By Tejal Rao

After a few days of intense, almost athletic eating and drinking with my family, I crave something delicious but basic. So after all the big, celebratory holiday dinners this week, and after several days of happily eating leftover pie for breakfast, it’ll be time for … a big pot of khichdi.";}s:8:"relation";a:1:{s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1637872120;}s:7:"creator";s:21:"Melissa Clepper-Faith";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:11:"last_change";a:8:{s:4:"date";i:1637872120;s:2:"ip";s:13:"98.192.76.251";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:15:"recipes:khichdi";s:4:"user";s:3:"mcf";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:2503;}}}